  "name": "Question 3",
  "problem": "The position vector $r$ of a particle $P$ (relative to a fixed origin $O$) at time $t$ is given by\n\n$$\nr=\u27e8\\operatorname{ln}\u2061({t}^{3}+2t),\\operatorname{ln}\u2061(9-{t}^{2})\u27e9,\\,t>0.\n$$\n\nCalculate the velocity vector $v.$\n\n$v=\u27e8${{field-1}}$,\\,-\\frac{2t}{9-{t}^{2}}\\,\u27e9$",
  "worked_solution": "The particle's velocity vector is given by the derivative of its position vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\u27e8\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t},\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e8\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{ln}\u2061({t}^{3}+2t)),\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{ln}\u2061(9-{t}^{2}))\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e8\\frac{3{t}^{2}+2}{{t}^{3}+2t},-\\frac{2t}{9-{t}^{2}}\u27e9\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
